# knowledge — accumulated knowledge

The third place for documentation in the repository, and each has its own nature. Do not mix them.

| Place | What it is | Who owns it |
|---|---|---|
| `{{ spec_path }}` | **Requirements and domain.** What the system must do. The source of truth. | The owner. Claude reads and asks, does not add. |
| `openspec/specs/` | **Implemented behavior** by capability. Derived from the spec. | OpenSpec, via `/opsx:propose` → `/opsx:apply` → `/opsx:archive`. |
| `knowledge/` | **Why it is so and what we found out.** Decisions with reasons, lessons, quirks of external APIs, open questions. | Shared. Grows as work goes on. |

Where does an entry go:

- "The system must …" — that is a requirement. It is either already in the spec or has to be asked of the owner. Not here.
- "On such-and-such input the system does …" — that is behavior. In `openspec/specs/`.
- "The external API returns at most N records, so we …" — here.
- "We chose X over Y because …" — here, as a file in `{{ decisions_path }}`.
- "Review found a defect, and here is what follows from it" — here, as a file in `{{ lessons_path }}`.
- "It is unclear how to count …" — here, in `{{ open_questions_path }}`, and in the stage report.

## What lives here

- `{{ decisions_path }}` — decisions, one file per decision. The format is in the directory README.
- `{{ lessons_path }}` — lessons, one file per lesson. The format is in the directory README.
- `{{ open_questions_path }}` — open questions with deadlines, in one file; closed ones go to `{{ open_questions_path[:-3] if open_questions_path.endswith('.md') else open_questions_path }}-closed.md`.
- `due.sh` — open questions whose deadline has come, by the stage table `{{ stages_path }}`; `--overdue` — overdue only (pre-push).
- `archive-questions.sh` — moves closed questions to the archive (pre-commit).
- `index.sh` — tables of contents of `{{ decisions_path }}/README.md` and `{{ lessons_path }}/README.md` between the markers (pre-commit).
- `tests/` — tests of the scripts; run on pre-push and in CI.
- `spec-unfolded.sh` — the list of spec revisions not yet folded into the sections; with `--write` it updates the block in the spec README. Test — `tests/spec-unfolded.sh`.
